  "Question": "Given the three numbers \\(x,\\) \\(y=x^x,\\) \\(z=x^{(x^x)},\\) with \\(0.9\\lt x\\lt1.0.\\) Arranged in order of increasing magnitude, they are:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(x,\\) \\(z,\\) \\(y\\)",
    "B": "\\(x,\\) \\(y,\\) \\(z\\)",
    "C": "\\(y,\\) \\(x,\\) \\(z\\)",
    "D": "\\(y,\\) \\(z,\\) \\(x\\)",
    "E": "\\(z,\\) \\(x,\\) \\(y\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "For the fixed value \\(x\\), the base satisfies \\(0<x<1\\), so \\(x^u\\) decreases as the exponent \\(u\\) increases. Comparing the exponents \\(0<x<1\\) first gives\n\\[\nx=x^1<x^x=y<x^0=1.\n\\]\nNow compare the exponents \\(x<y<1\\). The same decreasing-power rule reverses their order:\n\\[\nx=x^1<x^y=z<x^x=y.\n\\]\nThus the increasing order is \\(\\boxed{x,z,y}\\), choice A.",
